  "title": "Composing like cycles is affine structure modulo the tops",
  "subject": "Whether laws whose knots compose like cycles carry a Mal'tsev operation modulo the tops, what structure the tops carry, and which matroids such laws carry",
  "conclusion": "A law composes like cycles exactly when its ranges have tops, its ties are bijections modulo them, and a ternary polymorphism is Mal'tsev modulo the tops of its knot ranges, which proves the series' Conjecture 7 through rectangular top images. The tops of knot ranges are then elementary abelian p-groups with polymorphisms acting affinely, and every system carries a direct sum of matroids representable over finite fields, all of which occur.",
